{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under Rule 6c-11(d), an ETF must preserve:\n\n- **AP agreements:** Each written agreement between the ETF and an authorized participant (AP) that allows the AP to place creation or redemption orders. Retain the agreement **for at least five years after its termination**, with the **first two years** readily accessible.\n- **Basket records:** For each exchanged basket, retain a record of (1) the ticker symbol, CUSIP or other identifier, description, quantity, and weight of each holding; (2) cash balancing amounts; and (3) the AP that exchanged the basket. Keep these records **for at least five years**, with the **first two years** readily accessible.\n\nThese requirements apply to ETFs relying on Rule 6c-11."}}
